      "inputTokens": 98,
      "outputTokens": 722,
      "costUsd": 0.006547000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "First, take a cubic you've met before, y equals x cubed minus three x. It has a local maximum at minus one, two, a local minimum at one, minus two, and an inflection at the origin. Are those points enough? This wiggly curve goes through all three points. So does this one, made of straight lines. Both are wrong. What rules them out is what the derivatives say between the points: constraints, rules the curve has to obey."
    },
