      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 105,
      "outputTokens": 810,
      "costUsd": 0.007342499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Start with f prime. f prime of x is three, times x minus one, times x plus one. It's positive when x is less than minus one, negative between minus one and one, and positive again after one. So the curve must rise, then fall, then rise. Now look at the wiggly curve. Near zero it climbs, where f prime says it must fall. So it's out. Each sign of f prime is a rule for a whole interval, not just ay point."
    },
