      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 112,
      "outputTokens": 890,
      "costUsd": 0.008066,
      "pronunciationText": "Now pin it down. Symmetry. f of minus x is minus f of x, so the function is odd. Give the right half a half turn about the origin, and it lands exactly on the left half. Intercepts. x times x squared minus three is zero at zero, and at plus or minus root three, about one point seven three. And the ends. For large x, the x cubed term wins, so the curve heads up on the right, and down on the left. Label every feature, and only one shape fits."
