      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 139,
      "outputTokens": 1091,
      "costUsd": 0.0098885,
      "pronunciationText": "Sketch y equals x plus one over x. Domain first. x can't be zero, so the graph has a gap there, and comes in two separate pieces. It's odd, since f of minus x is minus f of x. There are no intercepts, because x plus one over x equals zero would need x squared equals minus one. f prime of x is x squared minus one, over x squared, which is zero at one and minus one. f double prime is two over x cubed. At one it's positive, so one, two is a local minimum. At minus one it's negative, so minus one, minus two is a local maximum."
    },
