      "inputTokens": 110,
      "outputTokens": 857,
      "costUsd": 0.007768000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Two over x cubed is negative on the left and positive on the right, so the concavity does change across zero. But zero isn't in the domain, so there's no point there, and no inflection. As x gets close to zero from the right, one over x grows without limit, so f heads up. From the left, it heads down. So x equals zero is a vertical asymptote. And as x gets large, one over x shrinks towards zero, so the curve gets closer to the line y equals x."
