      "inputTokens": 133,
      "outputTokens": 927,
      "costUsd": 0.0084095,
      "pronunciationText": "Now go the other way, from a graph of f with no formula. f prime is the gradient of f. Line the graphs up, one under the other. Where f turns, the tangent is flat, so f prime is zero. Where f rises, f prime is above the axis. Where f falls, it's below. And f is falling most steeply at the origin, so that's the lowest point on f prime. Now do it again. f double prime is the gradient of f prime. f prime falls until x equals zero, then rises, so f double prime is negative, then positive, crossing zero right under the inflection."
