      "inputTokens": 130,
      "outputTokens": 893,
      "costUsd": 0.008102000000000002,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's a new graph. At x equals three it turns, so f prime crosses the axis there, from negative to positive. But at the origin, the curve flattens and keeps falling. The tangent is flat, so f prime is zero, but its sign doesn't change. The graph of f prime touches the axis and goes back down. That's a horizontal point of inflection. The curve also changes its bend at x equals two, while it's still falling. There, f prime has a turning point. It also turns at zero, where it touches. So f double prime crosses zero at both points."
