      "costUsd": 0.0051315,
      "pronunciationText": "The domain is x not equal to zero, and f is odd. f prime of x is one plus four over x squared, which is always positive, so the curve rises on each piece and never turns. f double prime is minus eight over x cubed. It changes sign across zero, but zero isn't in the domain. No point, so no inflection."
