      "pronunciationText": "f is flat at minus one and at two, so f prime is zero there. At minus one, f turns from falling to rising, so f prime crosses. At two, f flattens but keeps rising, so f prime only touches. f prime turns where f changes its bend, at zero and at two. And f crossing the axis at zero doesn't make f prime zero there."
